Objective:

Enumerate an Active Directory environment from a low-privilege authenticated position —
mapping users, groups, computers, SPNs, and trust relationships to build an attack surface map.

Tools Used:

. impacket-GetADUsers — enumerate domain users
. impacket-GetUserSPNs — find Kerberoastable accounts (SPN-set)
. impacket-GetNPUsers — find AS-REP Roastable accounts (pre-auth disabled)
. netexec (formerly crackmapexec) — SMB/LDAP enumeration
. nmap — port scanning to identify AD services (88, 389, 445, 135, 3268)
. BloodHound (see separate BloodHound notes)

